
Somewhere way back in the 1990's it was clear to
me that the computation of a delta time between
to timespec data elements required a bit of thinking.
The data is NOT floating point. The data elements
are integers and thus we can not blindly convert
to floating point and hope for the best. We must
form a logic table of conditions and then compute
the time delta for each case. See the long comments
in the tdiff.c code. 

The code is ISO9899:1990 clean. Sure C99 works.

The test care output should look like : 

Case ( 1.1 ) tn_0 =        108    925000000
             tn_1 =        102    655000000
   expected delta = -6.27
            delta =         -6    270000000
             fp64 = -6.27               
 
Case ( 1.2 ) tn_0 =        277    186000000
             tn_1 =        192    186000000
   expected delta = -85.0
            delta =        -85            0
             fp64 = -85                 
 
Case ( 1.3 ) tn_0 =        126    587000000
             tn_1 =        104    816000000
   expected delta = -21.771
            delta =        -21    771000000
 
             fp64 = -21.771             
 
Case ( 2.1 ) tn_0 = 1718602045    843710014
             tn_1 = 1718602045    714047011
   expected delta = -0.129663003
            delta =          0    -129663003
 
             fp64 = -0.129663003        
 
Case ( 2.2 ) tn_0 = 1718668074    456789001
             tn_1 = 1718668074    456789001
   expected delta = 0.0
            delta =          0            0
 
             fp64 = +0                  
 
Case ( 2.3 ) tn_0 = 1718604178    149045751
             tn_1 = 1718604178    457419106
   expected delta = 0.308373355
            delta =          0    308373355
 
             fp64 = +0.308373355        
 
Case ( 3.1 ) tn_0 =      54387    390145701
             tn_1 =      68712    127084199
   expected delta = 14324.736938498
            delta =      14324    736938498
 
             fp64 = +14324.73694        
 
Case ( 3.2 ) tn_0 = 1718604178    123456789
             tn_1 = 1718604192    123456789
   expected delta = 14.0
            delta =         14            0
 
             fp64 = +14                 
 
Case ( 3.3 ) tn_0 = 1718604178     47684173
             tn_1 = 1718607011     94571341
