Wed Aug 14 21:46:01 GMT 2019

we play around with the leap year problem and 
determine what are valid dates and also how 
to set a locale inside software.

Fri Aug 16 23:49:03 GMT 2019

We covered UTF-8 options and then built three
code chunks to check for valid dates and also 
another to print out the locale aware date in
some strftime format. 

Please note the use of calloc() and mktime().


well into 2026 and I wanted a locale aware time report so
therefore locale_time.c exists. It can be tested with ALL
available locales on a machine thus : 

$ locale -a | awk 'BEGIN{print"#!/bin/sh\n\nIFS=\047 \t\n\047\n\n"}{print "./locale_time " $1 }' > test_locale_time.sh 
$ chmod 0755 test_locale_time.sh 

be sure to delete test_locale_time.sh afterwards

